## What the source says

`public-api.goldstandard.org` and `registry.goldstandard.org` both serve genuine
**404s for robots.txt**, so no crawl rules are stated — an absence of rules, not a
grant of rights. `www.goldstandard.org` permits everything except `/wp-admin/`,
`/wp-login.php`, `/wp-includes/` and `/preview/`. No AI agents are named anywhere.

Gold Standard's terms-and-conditions page addresses **trademarks** and media
captured at events. It says nothing about the project registry or reuse of the
API. So what Gold Standard permits for this data is **unknown to this repository**
as of **22 September 2026**, and an unknown is not a licence.

